<div class="footnotes text darkTableStyle aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12"><div class="footnote-container">
	<details>
		<summary>
			<div class="container ">
				<div class="row">
					<div class="col">
						<span class="label">Footnotes</span> <i class="fass fa-chevron-up"></i>
		</summary>
		<div class="footnote-details-container">
			<div class="container">
				<div class="row">
					<div class="col">
						<ol>
<li>Based on calculations by AMD Performance Labs in June 2026, for the AMD Helios Rackscale Solution to determine the peak theoretical performance when comparing peak Matrix FP16, BF16, INT8 and peak Open Compute Project MXFP6, MXFP8, FP8 and MXFP4 datatypes vs. NVIDIA Vera Rubin NVL72 (NVFP4 Dense). System manufacturers may vary configurations, yielding different results. MI400-005</li>
<li>Based on engineering projections by AMD performance labs in July 2026, to estimate peak theoretical precision performance of an AMD Instinct™ MI430X GPU using FP64 (Vector) datatype vs. AMD Instinct MI300X, NVIDIA B200, B300 and Vera Rubin GPUs with FP64 (Vector) datatype. Results subject to change when products are released in market. MI400-001C</li>
<li>Based on AMD Performance Labs calculations (June 2026) using an AMD Instinct™ MI455X GPU, peak theoretical performance (FP32, FP16, BF16, MXFP6, MXFP8, FP8, MXFP4 Matrix/Vector), compared to published specifications for AMD Instinct™ MI355X, MI350X, MI325X, MI300X, MI250X, and MI100 GPUs. Results may vary by system configuration and datatype. MI400-006</li>
<li>Calculations by AMD Performance Labs in June 2026, based on published memory capacity and memory bandwidth of AMD Instinct™ MI455X and MI430X GPU when comparing specifications vs. NVIDIA Vera Rubin GPU (NVFP4 Dense).  System manufacturers may vary configurations, yielding different results. MI400-004</li>
<li>Based on engineering projections by AMD performance labs in July 2026, to estimate peak theoretical precision performance of an AMD Instinct™ MI430X GPU using FP64 (Vector) datatype vs. NVIDIA Rubin GPU with FP64 (Vector) datatype. Results subject to change when products are released in market. MI400-001B</li>
</ol>

					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</details>
</div>

    
</div>

    
